DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((x+8))");
$fun_1 = Formula("sin((cos(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(10, infinity) U [3, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-7, -6, -2, -1, 4, 9})) U (10, infinity)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(10, infinity) U ({-7, -6, -2, -1, 4, 9} U {-7, -6, -2, -1, 4, 9} U [3, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (10, infinity))) U ([3, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - ([3, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, -6, -2, -1, 4, 9})))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, -6, -2, -1, 4, 9})");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("(10, infinity) U ([3, 12]) U ([3, 12] U (10, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, -6, -2, -1, 4, 9})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(1, infinity) U {-9, -8, -4, -1, 0, 7}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(1, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -8, -4, -1, 0, 7}) U ((1, infinity)) U (1, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (1, infinity))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-9, -8, -4, -1, 0, 7} U (1, infinity) U (1, infinity)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Lily was organizing her book collection. She had [`4`] shelves, each holding [`15`] books. Her brother had [`17`] shelves, each with [`13`] books. They decided to combine their collections into one big bookshelf. How many books do they have in total?

[_____]{281}
[%
4*15+17*13

First, calculate Lily's books: 4 × 15 = 60 books. Then, calculate her brother's books: 17 × 13 = 221 books. Finally, combine both collections: 60 + 221 = 281 books.
%]
---

During art class, Ms. Chen gave each of the [`8`] students a set of colored pencils to share. Unfortunately, all the pencils were used up in the previous class. Then she found a new box with [`19`] pencils and decided to give them all to one student who needed them most. How many pencils did that student receive?

[_____]{19}
[%
8*0+19/1

First, calculate the pencils from the shared sets: 8 × 0 = 0 pencils. Then, calculate the pencils from the new box: 19 ÷ 1 = 19 pencils. Finally, combine both amounts: 0 + 19 = 19 pencils.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -8, -4, -1, 0, 7\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap A \cup (B) \cup B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-7, -6, -2, -1, 4, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 12\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup C \cap (B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup (B \cup B \cup C \cap A) \cup (C \cap (C \cap B)) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`A \cup (C) \cup (C \cup A) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 9, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -9, 0, -7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -1, -6, 4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, 9, -6>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -6, 4>") x Compute("<3, 9, -6>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -6, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, 9, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, 0, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 3, 0 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 0, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 0, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 3, 0>") x Compute("<1, 0, 4>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 3, 0>") . Compute("<1, 0, 4>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, 0, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, 0, 4>") . Compute("<-5, 3, 0>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
